title: 'statement-store: resend statements a slow or failing peer missed'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    A peer that stops reading or whose sends fail no longer loses statements. A full
    propagation outbox now refuses new hashes instead of dropping its oldest, and a failed
    propagation send gives up its chunk and the hashes queued behind it, except detours. In
    both cases the peer records the lowest admission sequence it missed. Once its outbox drains
    and its last chunk completes, an initial sync walks the admission journal from that
    sequence to the current watermark, so the peer receives every missed statement. The walk
    may resend a statement the peer already has. Before, the dropped hashes and the failed
    chunks were never resent, and the peer got those statements only from another peer or a
    later full resync.

    Statements left to a walk now count in `send_failures` only, so
    `substrate_sync_statement_undelivered_total` counts statements no resync resends.

    On the v2 path the retention sweep can still remove a forwarded statement before the walk
    reaches it.
crates:
- name: sc-network-statement
  bump: patch
